      "message": "node: batch block file pruning in a single pass over block index\n\nWhen starting the node with pruning enabled (e.g. -prune=550) on a\nnode with full chain history or pruning many files at once,\nFindFilesToPrune and FindFilesToPruneManual previously called\nPruneOneBlockFile once per file.\n\nBecause PruneOneBlockFile iterated over the entire m_block_index for\neach file, this was an O(M * N) operation (M = files to prune,\nN = total blocks). When pruning a full chain (~5,770 files and ~972k\nblocks), this triggered ~5.6 billion iterations and froze the node\nfor ~10 minutes on startup while holding cs_main.\n\nReplace PruneOneBlockFile with PruneBlockFiles(const std::set<int>&),\nwhich collects all candidate files and prunes them in a single O(M + N)\npass over m_block_index using a compact dynamic bitfield\n(std::vector<bool>). Also skip entries without block or undo data to\navoid unneeded checks and prevent file 0 pruning from dirtying\nheader-only or already-pruned index entries.\n\nBenchmarked with ~972k blocks and 5,770 files to prune:\n- x86_64 (i7-8665U @ 1.90 GHz): 75.1s -> 14.7ms (~5,100x speedup)\n- ARM64 (Raspberry Pi 5): 606.0s -> 26.3ms (>3,500x speedup)\n\nAdd unit test blockmanager_prune_block_files_batch to verify batch\npruning, empty set no-ops, and clean dirty-set behavior. Update\ncaller tests in blockmanager_tests and rescan_tests.",
